            <ArticleTitle>Coronary arterial anatomy in patients with left ventricular systolic dysfunction without chest pain or previous myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1530-1, A7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients with left ventricular systolic dysfunction without chest pain or previous myocardial infarction are unlikely to have 3-vessel coronary artery disease and are very unlikely to have coronary anatomy suitable for bypass grafting. Of our 108 subjects, only 3 (3%) had 3-vessel coronary artery disease thought to be suitable for revascularization.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
